<title>USA: Converse says cannot explain shr activity.</title>
<headline>Converse says cannot explain shr activity.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH READING, Mass. 1997-05-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Converse Inc said that it knows of no corporate developments that would explain Friday's market activity in its common stock, other than the announcement earlier in the day of the public offering of $70 million in seven percent convertible subordinated notes.</p>
<p>The company's shares closed up 2-1/4 at $20 on volume of 1.58 million shares on Friday.</p>
<p>The $70 million principal amount was a $10 million increase over the previously announced size of the offering, Converse said.</p>
<p>The notes are due June 1, 2004.</p>
</text>
